  "details": "\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: An executable file with some well-known name like zip,\n      gzip, and so on can be started from a current directory during some\n      plugin is opening apropriate file that has a one of the extensions .zip,\n      .gzip, .rb, and etc. This issue is effective only if the PATH\n      environment variable has a ./ (dot) as one element in the path list\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2023-4736.patch: avoid starting executable from\n       a current directory for some plugins\n     - CVE-2023-4736",
